# SPA fallback, in Netlify's format.
#
# The app is a single-page bundle: React Router owns every path, but a host
# only ever has index.html on disk. Without a fallback a visitor landing
# straight on /about — from a link, a bookmark or a search result — asks for a
# file that does not exist and gets a 404. Only / works, because only / is a
# real file.
#
# Each host needs this said in its own dialect, and none of them read another's:
#
#   Netlify, Cloudflare Pages   this file
#   Vercel                      vercel.json -> rewrites
#   GitHub Pages                a copy of index.html named 404.html
#   Apache / Nginx              try_files, or an ErrorDocument at index.html
#
# The Vercel rewrite excludes /api/ so the inquiry function still answers there
# rather than being handed the HTML page. It carries no comment of its own:
# vercel.json is validated against a strict schema that rejects any key it does
# not recognise, including the "//" convention, so the reasoning lives here.

/*  /index.html  200
